From c35f14f3ab5cb65094863b9a0e888370b027a670 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] llm: refresh sampler after runtime generation config changes

MNN 3.5.0 creates its sampler in Llm::load().  A later set_config() merges
per-request generation settings but previously left that sampler unchanged.
Consequently a request reported as greedy could still execute with the model
package's original mixed sampler.  Recreate only an already-existing sampler;
pre-load configuration keeps the normal load path unchanged.

---
 transformers/llm/engine/src/llm.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/transformers/llm/engine/src/llm.cpp b/transformers/llm/engine/src/llm.cpp
index 0834bb6..9950d75 100644
--- a/transformers/llm/engine/src/llm.cpp
+++ b/transformers/llm/engine/src/llm.cpp
@@ -125,6 +125,13 @@ bool Llm::set_config(const std::string& content) {
             mBlockSize = mValidBlockSize[mValidBlockSize.size()-1];
         } while (false);
     }
+    // The sampler is created by load(), but generation options are commonly
+    // changed between requests. Rebuild an existing sampler so those options
+    // (especially greedy vs. mixed sampling) take effect immediately instead
+    // of continuing to use the package's initial sampler configuration.
+    if (mSampler != nullptr) {
+        mSampler.reset(Sampler::createSampler(mContext, mConfig));
+    }
     return true;
 }
